# StudyHub AI — React Native (Expo) App

A real React Native app built with Expo, matching the Figma high-fidelity wireframes.
This is a **different codebase** from the earlier HTML/CSS/JS version — this one is a
proper mobile app you run through Expo Go, not a browser.

## Requirements
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) installed (LTS version)
- The free **Expo Go** app installed on your phone (App Store / Google Play)
- Your phone and computer on the **same Wi-Fi network**

## How to run it

1. Unzip this folder and open a terminal inside it.
2. Install dependencies (only needed once):
   ```
   npm install
   ```
3. Start the Expo development server:
   ```
   npx expo start
   ```
4. A QR code will appear in the terminal (and a browser tab).
   - **iPhone:** open the Camera app and point it at the QR code, tap the
     notification that appears.
   - **Android:** open the **Expo Go** app and tap "Scan QR code."
5. The app will build and load on your phone — start from the Splash screen.

If you want to test in a simulator/emulator instead of a real phone:
```
npx expo start --ios       (Mac only, needs Xcode)
npx expo start --android   (needs Android Studio)
```

